  year={2016},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={VII-IX},
  abstract={Integration of functional safety operations are becoming more and more relevant for the current and intelligent future applications. Collaborative robots, virtual fences and autonomous driving are paving the way for more intelligent and faster certification process where safety is not a by-product. Traditional homogeneous architectures requires often require prohibitive or extremely expensive evaluation of common more causes and systematic errors, that make such intelligent system very difficult to certify. Heterogeneous computing system like Zynq7000 that merge standard processor, soft processors, and programmable logic as combination of integrated hardware and software diversity under the same environment foster the way for high performance and safety oriented architecture. The keynote will report on the methodology and trend to achieve such new design.},
