  abstract={Summary <p>Silicon&#x2010;printed electronics (PE) integration is demonstrated by the application example of intelligent packaging. Silicon microcontroller unit (MCU) and light&#x2010;emitting displays (LEDs) are integrated with printed conductive patterns and humidity sensors on flexible substrates. A humidity sensor box is proposed as an example of a smart package that communicates with the environment and the user. The plastic&#x2010;based humidity sensor box prototype is implemented by integrating the MCU, LED arrays, functionalized multiwalled carbon nanotubes (f&#x2010;MWCNT)&#x2010;based resistive sensor, and discrete components. The plastic&#x2010;based system is embedded in the product package and interacts with the end&#x2010;user through the open window. The plastic&#x2010;based humidity sensor box gains sensing functionality by embedding the flexible electronic system inside the product packages. Using paper as the substrate enables merging of the manufacture of electronics into the normal package fabrication process and thereby reduces the number of manufacturing steps and further lowers the cost.</p>},
